+  <p>The other readouts:</p>
+  <ul>
+    <li><strong>Vestigial jobs.</strong> Extra jobs born no later than the main job and shrinking late in training are 3.5% of non-main clusters (2.6–4.4%). So extra jobs are not, in the main, leftovers from early training <span class="src">spec §11</span>.</li>
+    <li><strong>Replacement.</strong> In 17 poles, 2.8% of 600, the final main job is late-born and the judge was right on at most one of its four judgments <span class="src">spec §11</span>.</li>
+    <li><strong>The hard decoy.</strong> This check asks whether the judge reads more than the topic, using the same-layer pole with the most similar strongest tokens. Even on the controls, the judge beat it only 79.8% of the time, below the 0.80 floor, so the row is not measurable <span class="src">spec §11</span>. The study therefore cannot rule out that the judge partly matched records by topic.</li>
+  </ul>
