 <section id="meaning">
-  <h2>What each result would mean</h2>
+  <h2>What the result means</h2>
+  <p>By the rule, packing: of the jobs born after a pole’s first job, an estimated quarter, 21–32%, are unrelated to the pole’s top-20 record at the checkpoint before their birth, as far as this judge can tell. Recursive generalization, as the spec states it, allows fewer than one in ten <span class="src">spec §1</span>. In the same poles, extra jobs are rarely leftovers and wholesale replacement is rare. The two readouts do not contradict each other: by the estimate most late-born jobs have a parent in the pole, and the main job is born first more often than chance (47.6% of poles, against 41.4% under random order), but about a quarter of late-born jobs arrive without one.</p>
+  <p>The decision written before any data says: if Q2 lands for packing, the next five studies keep decomposition methods, and the neuron basis becomes one view among several <span class="src">spec §1</span>.</p>
+  <p>What the result does not settle:</p>
   <ul>
-    <li><strong>Recursive generalization holds.</strong> This would be the first independent, checkpoint-level evidence for the essay’s mechanism, on a 2025 open model. The next studies would use the network’s own neurons as the unit.</li>
-    <li><strong>Packing holds.</strong> This would be the first evidence against the mechanism at this scale. The next studies would keep decomposition methods, with neurons as one view among several.</li>
-    <li><strong>Mixed.</strong> It is reported with its point estimate. No rule is reinterpreted after unblinding <span class="src">spec §6.7</span>.</li>
-    <li><strong>The judge fails its control.</strong> The parent test is reported as not valid. Birth order is still read.</li>
+    <li><strong>The hard-decoy row was not measurable</strong>: the judge’s control accuracy against that decoy was 0.798, below 0.80. So a judge that matches records partly by topic is not ruled out.</li>
+    <li><strong>One model and one corpus.</strong> The development test ran on OLMo-3-1025-7B only, over a 20.57M-token corpus at 16 checkpoints.</li>
+    <li><strong>The serving changed.</strong> The clusterer and judge were the gated Sonnet 5.5 with the gated prompts. The judge and 883 of the 1,200 clustering answers were served through Claude Code without constrained decoding, not through the API <span class="src">RESULTS.md footnotes</span>. The predictions had assumed a different model, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash.</li>
   </ul>
-  <p>In the audit, a not-understood pole says something about the explainer and the test, never about packing <span class="src">spec §0b</span>. The models have 4 to 7 billion parameters, and the corpus is 200 times smaller than the essay’s 10 billion tokens. The study predicts it will not reach the essay’s 90 / 7 / 2–4, and it will examine any gap on the observer’s side first <span class="src">journal 20 Oct 02:58Z</span>.</p>
